<h3 class="font-headline-sm text-primary">IV & Surgical Treatment</h3>
</div>
<ul class="space-y-6">
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">IV Antibiotics (Hospital)</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">IV ampicillin-sulbactam or clindamycin for moderate-severe facial cellulitis, rapidly spreading redness, or orbital involvement. Upgraded based on culture results. <a href="/Facial-Swellings/soft-tissue-infection-treatment-hyderabad" class="text-secondary underline">Soft tissue infection treatment</a> covers severe cases.</p></li>
<li><h4 class="font-semibold text-primary mb-2">Drainage (if abscess forms)</h4><p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm">If ultrasound reveals an abscess within the cellulitis, surgical incision and drainage is required alongside antibiotics. Waiting for the abscess to "resolve with antibiotics alone" risks worsening.</p></li>
</ul>
